{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdWKLWGoDyChqkjVSnVQh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019MZpiXKcrYWYun8pjS97UQ","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/analysis/IMPACT_REPORT.md","content":"# Dependency Graph Impact Report: tonic → hyper → tokio\n\n**Repos analyzed:**\n- `/workspace/tonic` — tonic v0.6.0 (gRPC)\n- `/workspace/hyper` — hyper v0.14.0 (HTTP/1 & HTTP/2)\n- `/workspace/tokio` — tokio 1.0.0 (async runtime)\n\n---\n\n## 1. Dependency Chain with Exact Version Constraints\n\n### 1.1 tonic → hyper / tokio (declared in `/workspace/tonic/tonic/Cargo.toml`)\n\n```toml\n[features]\ntransport = [\"h2\", \"hyper\", \"tokio\", \"tower\", \"tracing-futures\", \"tokio/macros\", \"tokio/time\", \"hyper-timeout\"]\n\n[dependencies]\nh2       = { version = \"0.3\",     optional = true }\nhyper    = { version = \"0.14.4\",  features = [\"full\"], optional = true }\ntokio    = { version = \"1.0.1\",   features = [\"net\"],  optional = true }\ntokio-stream = \"0.1\"\ntokio-util   = { version = \"0.6\", features = [\"codec\"] }\ntower    = { version = \"0.4.7\", features = [\"balance\",\"buffer\",\"discover\",\"limit\",\"load\",\"make\",\"timeout\",\"util\"], optional = true }\n```\n\nKey points (`/workspace/tonic/tonic/Cargo.toml:34-43,61,73-79`):\n- tonic's default feature set (`default = [\"transport\", \"codegen\", \"prost\"]`, line 28) pulls in `hyper`, `tokio`, `h2`, `tower` unconditionally for any typical build.\n- tonic requires **hyper `^0.14.4`** (i.e. `>=0.14.4, <0.15.0`) with `features = [\"full\"]`.\n- tonic requires **tokio `^1.0.1`** (i.e. `>=1.0.1, <2.0.0`) directly, with feature `net`, plus `tokio/macros` and `tokio/time` enabled via the `transport` feature.\n- tonic also requires `tokio-util ^0.6` (feature `codec`) and `tokio-stream ^0.1` — both are workspace members of the tokio repo, not the `tokio` crate itself.\n- tonic requires `h2 ^0.3` directly (in addition to the copy hyper pulls in for HTTP/2).\n\nDirect tokio usage inside tonic source (not just via hyper): `tokio::net::TcpStream` (`/workspace/tonic/tonic/src/transport/server/conn.rs:3`), `impl Connected for tokio::io::DuplexStream` (`/workspace/tonic/tonic/src/transport/server/conn.rs:101`), and `tokio::net::UnixListener`/`UnixStream` in example/test code.\n\n### 1.2 hyper → tokio (declared in `/workspace/hyper/Cargo.toml`)\n\n```toml\n[dependencies]\ntokio = { version = \"1\", features = [\"sync\"] }\n\n[features]\nfull    = [\"client\", \"http1\", \"http2\", \"server\", \"stream\", \"runtime\"]\nruntime = [\"tcp\", \"tokio/rt\"]\ntcp     = [\"socket2\", \"tokio/net\", \"tokio/rt\", \"tokio/time\"]\n```\n\n(`/workspace/hyper/Cargo.toml:36`, `76-107`)\n\n- hyper's *base* dependency on tokio is `^1.0` with only the `sync` feature enabled unconditionally.\n- Enabling hyper's `tcp` feature (pulled in transitively by `runtime`, which is pulled in by `full`) additionally activates `tokio/net`, `tokio/rt`, and `tokio/time`.\n- Because tonic enables `hyper = { features = [\"full\"] }`, the *effective* tokio feature set required through hyper is: **`sync`, `net`, `rt`, `time`**.\n\n### 1.3 tonic → tokio, feature union\n\nCombining tonic's direct requirement (`net`, plus `macros`/`time` via the `transport` feature) with hyper's transitive requirement (`sync`, `net`, `rt`, `time`), a full tonic build with the `transport` feature needs tokio built with at least:\n\n```\nsync, net, rt, time, macros\n```\n\nAll satisfied by tokio's `full` feature superset (`/workspace/tokio/tokio/Cargo.toml:31-44`), but not by tokio's `default = []` (line 28) — tonic and hyper both rely on the consumer/build to opt in via non-default features, since tokio ships with **no default features**.\n\n### 1.4 Full chain diagram\n\n```\ntonic 0.6.0\n ├─ hyper  ^0.14.4  (feature \"full\")───► tokio ^1  (feature \"sync\", + \"net\",\"rt\",\"time\" via \"full\"→\"runtime\"→\"tcp\")\n ├─ tokio  ^1.0.1    (feature \"net\", + \"macros\",\"time\" via tonic's \"transport\" feature)\n ├─ tokio-util ^0.6  (feature \"codec\")   [tokio-rs/tokio workspace member]\n ├─ tokio-stream ^0.1                    [tokio-rs/tokio workspace member]\n ├─ h2 ^0.3                              [also a transitive dep of hyper's \"http2\" feature]\n └─ tower ^0.4.7                         [not a tokio/hyper dependency in this graph]\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. tokio APIs hyper Uses That tonic Depends On Transitively\n\nGrep of `tokio::` usage across hyper's production source (`/workspace/hyper/src/**`, excluding tests/benches/examples) shows these modules, all reachable from tonic once it enables `hyper = { features = [\"full\"] }`:\n\n| hyper source file | tokio API used | tokio feature required |\n|---|---|---|\n| `/workspace/hyper/src/common/drain.rs:4` | `tokio::sync::watch` | `sync` |\n| `/workspace/hyper/src/client/dispatch.rs:5` | `tokio::sync::{mpsc, oneshot}` | `sync` |\n| `/workspace/hyper/src/upgrade.rs:15-16` | `tokio::io::{AsyncRead, AsyncWrite, ReadBuf}`, `tokio::sync::oneshot` | `sync` (io traits are feature-independent) |\n| `/workspace/hyper/src/common/io/rewind.rs:5` | `tokio::io::{AsyncRead, AsyncWrite, ReadBuf}` | — |\n| `/workspace/hyper/src/server/mod.rs:69` | `tokio::io::{AsyncRead, AsyncWrite}` | — |\n| `/workspace/hyper/src/server/conn.rs:58` | `tokio::io::{AsyncRead, AsyncWrite}` (doc examples show `tokio::net::TcpListener`, `tokio::task::spawn`) | `rt` (spawn), `net` (doc) |\n| `/workspace/hyper/src/server/tcp.rs:6-7` (`#[cfg(feature = \"tcp\")]`, `/workspace/hyper/src/server/mod.rs:57-58`) | `tokio::net::TcpListener`, `tokio::time::Sleep`, `tokio::net::TcpStream` | `net`, `time` |\n| `/workspace/hyper/src/client/connect/http.rs:15-16` (`#[cfg(feature = \"tcp\")]`, `/workspace/hyper/src/client/connect/mod.rs:87-90`) | `tokio::net::{TcpSocket, TcpStream}`, `tokio::time::Sleep` | `net`, `time` |\n| `/workspace/hyper/src/client/connect/dns.rs:32` | `tokio::task::JoinHandle` | `rt` |\n| `/workspace/hyper/src/client/pool.rs:11` (`#[cfg(feature = \"runtime\")]`) | `tokio::time::{Duration, Instant, Interval}` | `time` |\n| `/workspace/hyper/src/client/connect/mod.rs:267` | `tokio::io::{AsyncRead, AsyncWrite}` (sealed `Connection` trait bound) | — |\n\nFeature gating confirmed in hyper's own source: `#[cfg(feature = \"tcp\")]` guards `mod tcp` in `/workspace/hyper/src/server/mod.rs:57-58`, the `HttpConnector`/`dns` modules in `/workspace/hyper/src/client/connect/mod.rs:86-91`, and `AddrIncoming`/`AddrStream` re-exports in `/workspace/hyper/src/server/conn.rs:79-80`.\n\nSince tonic's `transport` feature builds hyper with `features = [\"full\"]` (`/workspace/tonic/tonic/Cargo.toml:74`), **all of the above tokio surfaces (`sync`, `net`, `rt`, `time`) are reachable from tonic**, meaning any breaking change to `tokio::net::{TcpStream, TcpListener, TcpSocket}`, `tokio::time::{Sleep, Interval}`, `tokio::sync::{oneshot, mpsc, watch}`, `tokio::task::{spawn, JoinHandle}`, or the `AsyncRead`/`AsyncWrite`/`ReadBuf` traits in tokio directly impacts hyper's public API surface, and therefore tonic's `transport::Server`/`transport::Channel` types built on top of it (e.g. `/workspace/tonic/tonic/src/transport/server/conn.rs`, `/workspace/tonic/tonic/src/transport/channel/endpoint.rs:263-289` which constructs `hyper::client::connect::HttpConnector`).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Version Pinning Conflicts Across the Three Repos\n\n### 3.1 hyper version mismatch (real conflict)\n\n- `/workspace/tonic/tonic/Cargo.toml:74` requires: `hyper = { version = \"0.14.4\", features = [\"full\"] }` → Cargo semver range `>=0.14.4, <0.15.0`.\n- `/workspace/hyper/Cargo.toml:3` declares: `version = \"0.14.0\"`.\n- **0.14.0 does not satisfy `^0.14.4`.** If this checked-out hyper tree were used as a local `path`/`[patch]` override for tonic's build without also bumping hyper's own `version` field (no `[patch]` section exists in either repo's `Cargo.toml` — confirmed via search), Cargo would reject the resolution: the local hyper crate is *older* than tonic's stated minimum. In a normal crates.io-based build, Cargo would instead pull hyper `0.14.4+` from the registry, silently bypassing the local hyper checkout — meaning the three repos as checked out are **not mutually consistent** for local/offline/patched builds.\n\n### 3.2 tokio version mismatch (real conflict)\n\n- `/workspace/tonic/tonic/Cargo.toml:76` requires: `tokio = { version = \"1.0.1\", features = [\"net\"] }` → Cargo semver range `>=1.0.1, <2.0.0`.\n- `/workspace/tokio/tokio/Cargo.toml:11` declares: `version = \"1.0.0\"`.\n- **1.0.0 does not satisfy `^1.0.1`.** Same failure mode as §3.1: a local path/patch override of this tokio tree against tonic would fail to resolve; a registry-based build would silently substitute a newer tokio (≥1.0.1) instead of the checked-out 1.0.0 tree.\n- hyper's own tokio requirement (`/workspace/hyper/Cargo.toml:36`, `tokio = { version = \"1\", features = [\"sync\"] }` → `>=1.0.0, <2.0.0`) **is** satisfied by the local tokio 1.0.0 tree, so this specific mismatch is isolated to the **tonic→tokio** edge, not hyper→tokio.\n\n### 3.3 No-default-features trap (latent/behavioral conflict)\n\n- tokio ships `default = []` (`/workspace/tokio/tokio/Cargo.toml:28`) — no functionality is enabled unless a consumer opts in.\n- tonic's `transport` feature only turns on `tokio/net`, `tokio/macros`, `tokio/time` (`/workspace/tonic/tonic/Cargo.toml:34-43`) and hyper's `full` only turns on `tokio/rt` + `tcp` (`net`,`rt`,`time`) (`/workspace/hyper/Cargo.toml:98-107`). Neither turns on `tokio/rt-multi-thread`. Any tonic/hyper consumer that also wants `#[tokio::main]` with a multi-threaded runtime, or `tokio::task::spawn_blocking`-heavy workloads, must add `rt-multi-thread`/other features explicitly at the top-level binary crate — this is not a version conflict but a **feature-unification gap** that silently changes runtime behavior (single-thread current-thread runtime vs. multi-thread) depending on what the final binary crate enables.\n\n### 3.4 Non-conflicting sibling crates (checked, consistent)\n\n- `tokio-util` — tonic requires `^0.6` (features `[\"codec\"]`), local tokio-repo workspace member `tokio-util` is at `0.6.0` (`/workspace/tokio/tokio-util/Cargo.toml:10`) → **satisfies**.\n- `tokio-stream` — tonic requires `^0.1`, local tokio-repo workspace member is at `0.1.0` (`/workspace/tokio/tokio-stream/Cargo.toml:10`) → **satisfies**.\n- `h2` — tonic requires `^0.3` directly (`/workspace/tonic/tonic/Cargo.toml:73`) and hyper's optional `h2` dependency is also `^0.3` (`/workspace/hyper/Cargo.toml:31`) → **compatible**, single `h2` version resolves for both.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Nature of Each Change / Risk Summary\n\n| Edge | Constraint | Local pin | Nature | Impact |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| tonic → hyper | `^0.14.4` | `0.14.0` | **Version-pin conflict** (patch-level) | Local hyper tree too old to satisfy tonic; registry build silently resolves to a different hyper than what's checked out locally, defeating reproducible/offline builds. |\n| tonic → tokio | `^1.0.1` | `1.0.0` | **Version-pin conflict** (patch-level) | Same failure mode; local tokio tree too old for tonic's direct requirement. |\n| hyper → tokio | `^1` (feature `sync`) | `1.0.0` | Satisfied | No conflict on this edge alone. |\n| tonic/hyper → tokio feature set | needs `sync,net,rt,time,macros` | tokio `default=[]` | **Feature-unification gap** (behavioral, not a version conflict) | Must be explicitly enabled by the final binary; omission causes compile errors or degraded (single-thread) runtime behavior, not a version error. |\n| tonic → tokio-util / tokio-stream / h2 | `^0.6` / `^0.1` / `^0.3` | `0.6.0` / `0.1.0` / `0.3` (via hyper) | Satisfied | No conflict. |\n\nNone of the tokio APIs hyper uses (`tokio::sync::{oneshot,mpsc,watch}`, `tokio::net::{TcpStream,TcpListener,TcpSocket}`, `tokio::time::{Sleep,Interval,Instant}`, `tokio::task::{spawn,JoinHandle}`, `tokio::io::{AsyncRead,AsyncWrite,ReadBuf}`) show signature/removal differences between what tokio 1.0.0 exposes and what hyper 0.14.0's source calls — the conflicts identified are **manifest-level version pins**, not API breakage, at this specific commit trio.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Upgrade Coordination Strategy\n\n1. **Fix the two patch-level pin conflicts first, before any feature/API work:**\n   - Bump the local tokio checkout's workspace version to at least `1.0.1` (or point tonic/hyper's `Cargo.lock` at a real `1.0.1+` release) so tonic's `tokio = \"1.0.1\"` requirement resolves against the local tree.\n   - Bump the local hyper checkout to at least `0.14.4` (or re-point tonic at the actual 0.14.4 release) so tonic's `hyper = \"0.14.4\"` requirement resolves.\n   - If these repos are meant to be built together locally (e.g. via `[patch.crates-io]` or path dependencies), add explicit `[patch]` sections in tonic's workspace `Cargo.toml` pinning `hyper` and `tokio` to the local paths — currently **no `[patch]` section exists in tonic's repo**, so there is nothing overriding the registry resolution today.\n\n2. **Upgrade order (bottom-up, since tokio is the foundation both hyper and tonic build on):**\n   1. `tokio` (and its workspace siblings `tokio-util`, `tokio-stream`) — verify `sync`, `net`, `rt`, `time`, `macros` feature APIs (`AsyncRead`/`AsyncWrite`/`ReadBuf`, `TcpStream`/`TcpListener`/`TcpSocket`, `oneshot`/`mpsc`/`watch`, `spawn`/`JoinHandle`, `Sleep`/`Interval`/`Instant`) remain source-compatible with hyper's usage sites listed in §2.\n   2. `hyper` — re-run hyper's own test suite (`/workspace/hyper/tests/{client,server,integration}.rs`) against the new tokio to catch any behavioral regressions in the `tcp`/`runtime` feature-gated code paths before touching tonic.\n   3. `tonic` — re-run `tonic/tests/integration_tests` and `tonic/tests/compression` (both exercise `tokio::io::DuplexStream`/`tokio::net::TcpListener` end-to-end through hyper's transport) plus tonic-web/tonic-reflection integration tests.\n\n3. **Pin discipline going forward:** since tonic pins tighter lower bounds than hyper (`tokio ^1.0.1` vs hyper's `tokio ^1`; `hyper ^0.14.4` exactly), any coordinated bump should update tonic's `Cargo.toml` lower bounds to match whatever minimum hyper/tokio version the new API usage actually requires, rather than leaving stale minimums that silently pass because the registry substitutes newer versions — the same trap that produced the two conflicts in §3.1–3.2.\n\n4. **Feature-set audit:** when bumping, explicitly re-verify hyper's `full` feature still maps to `tcp → tokio/net + tokio/rt + tokio/time` and that tonic's `transport` feature still maps to `tokio/net + tokio/macros + tokio/time` (`/workspace/tonic/tonic/Cargo.toml:34-43`, `/workspace/hyper/Cargo.toml:98-107`) — a tokio feature rename/split (e.g. splitting `net` into `net-tcp`/`net-unix`) would be a silent breaking change to both hyper's and tonic's `Cargo.toml` feature arrays without bumping tonic's or hyper's own semver, so feature-flag diffs deserve the same scrutiny as symbol-level API diffs.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":72313,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":59,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"37b6ba6b-4eee-49b4-9ad5-211eb40d4828","uuid":"3e49cb7c-161a-4177-af3c-b13f54903335","timestamp":"2026-07-29T12:05:09.790Z","request_id":"req_011CdWKLU5LwrcERbZ9xe95C"}
